# Line endings (D7).
#
# A Windows checkout with the default `core.autocrlf` rewrites every text file
# on the way to disk. Without this file the behaviour is whatever the runner's
# git happens to be configured for, which is exactly the kind of thing that
# produces a failure nobody can reproduce.
#
# Three things in this repository read bytes and compare them, and all three
# break under CRLF:
#
#   - `gen/generate.jl --check`, which compares generated output byte-for-byte
#     against what is checked in;
#   - `JuliaFormatter.format(".")`, likewise;
#   - the hermetic tests that read a fixture and compare its text, which unlike
#     the first two run on all three platforms.
#
# So: LF in the repository and LF in the working tree, everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ...except where the bytes are the point. `text=auto` guesses, and a guess
# that goes wrong on a binary corrupts it silently. These say don't guess.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.webm binary
*.mp4 binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.xz binary
*.tgz binary

# test/fixtures/api.har.zip is the one binary fixture tracked today: a HAR
# recording that the replay tests hand to the driver unmodified. Covered by
# `*.zip` above; named here because it is the file that would actually break.
*.har.zip binary
